## Set up

Payments is optional: only if clients pay you through LogIt. Payments › Packages walks you through
three steps: connect Stripe (Stripe's own sign-up; what it asks for depends on your country), make a
package, and offer it when someone asks to be coached. You're the seller: your own VAT. Stripe's card
fees are yours; LogIt takes nothing.

When you come back from Stripe, Packages shows where you are: ready to take payments, Stripe still
checking your details, or setup not finished (what you entered is kept). If Stripe needs something
months later, it's first on Today and offers say they can't be paid until you finish in Stripe.

Packages work without Stripe too: they show on your profile, and an offer can say "No payment through
LogIt". Clients pay on Stripe's page, where they can type a discount code you made under Coupons in your
Stripe dashboard. You get an email when someone pays.

## Changing, refunding, stopping

Manage on a row in Payments › Clients:

- **Change package** sends the client an offer card in your conversation. Nothing changes until they
  accept, and the change starts at their next payment, so nobody pays twice.
- **Refund** gives money back through your Stripe account; coaching carries on. Stripe's fee on the
  original payment isn't returned to you.
- **Pause or end coaching** opens the client's page, where ending can refund too.

A payment disputed with the client's bank shows as Disputed; it changes nothing on its own. You answer
it in Stripe.

To leave Stripe, Payments › Settings › Stop taking payments through LogIt. Plans stop renewing, each
client keeps coaching to the end of what they paid for, then shows as paid elsewhere. Nothing is
refunded, and your Stripe account stays yours.

## When a payment fails

LogIt emails the client a link to update their card, and Stripe tries the card again over a few days.
Clients can also press Update card in My coach on the web; Stripe takes the overdue payment as soon as the
new card is in. You choose what happens to coaching meanwhile, for everyone or per client, and you get an
email too; turn these off in Payments › Settings.

